@subsection Burgermistress Statement: Assignment

@cindex Burgermistress assignment

Assignment statements modify variable values.

@strong{Syntax}:
@example
VariableName = Expression
@end example

@strong{Example 1: Simple Assignment**:
@example
Health = 100
Damage = 25
@end example

@strong{Example 2: Assignment with Expression**:
@example
TotalDamage = WeaponDamage + BonusDamage
NewHealth = CurrentHealth - Damage
@end example

@strong{Example 3: Assignment with Different Types**:
@example
Flags = 0B1010
Counter = 0
MaxValue = 255
@end example

@strong{Example 4: Assignment in Condition**:
@example
IF Health > 0 THEN
  NewHealth = Health - 25
  Health = NewHealth
END IF
@end example

@strong{Example 5: Assignment in Loop**:
@example
Counter = 0
DO WHILE Counter < 10
  Process(Counter)
  Counter = Counter + 1
LOOP
@end example

@strong{Domain-Specific Features}:
Burgermistress assignments support complex expressions with automatic type conversion.
Assignments are typically optimized to direct register or memory writes. Multiple numeric
types can be mixed in assignment expressions with transparent conversion.

