@subsection Burgermistress Statement: DO-LOOP

@cindex Burgermistress DO-LOOP

The DO-LOOP statement implements iteration with optional conditions.

@strong{Syntax}:
@example
DO [WHILE condition | UNTIL condition]
  statements
LOOP
@end example

@strong{Example 1: Simple Loop**:
@example
DO
  UpdateGame()
  RenderFrame()
LOOP
@end example

@strong{Example 2: While Loop**:
@example
Counter = 0
DO WHILE Counter < 10
  Print Counter
  Counter = Counter + 1
LOOP
@end example

@strong{Example 3: Until Loop**:
@example
DO UNTIL PlayerDead
  UpdateEnemies()
  CheckPlayerHealth()
LOOP
@end example

@strong{Example 4: Loop with Break**:
@example
Counter = 0
DO
  Process(Counter)
  Counter = Counter + 1
  IF Counter >= 100 THEN
    EXIT DO
  END IF
LOOP
@end example

@strong{Example 5: Nested Loops**:
@example
X = 0
DO WHILE X < 10
  Y = 0
  DO WHILE Y < 10
    ProcessCell(X, Y)
    Y = Y + 1
  LOOP
  X = X + 1
LOOP
@end example

@strong{Domain-Specific Features}:
DO-LOOP generates compact iteration code suitable for 8-bit platforms. WHILE conditions
enable efficient continue-while patterns. UNTIL conditions provide clear exit semantics
for finite-duration loops. The compiler can optimize numeric loop conditions to
countdown loops.

