@subsection Burgermistress Statement: FOR Loop

@cindex Burgermistress FOR loop

The FOR statement implements counted iteration.

@strong{Syntax}:
@example
FOR LoopVariable = StartValue TO EndValue [STEP StepValue]
  statements
NEXT [LoopVariable]
@end example

@strong{Example 1: Simple FOR Loop**:
@example
FOR I = 1 TO 10
  Print I
NEXT
@end example

@strong{Example 2: FOR with STEP**:
@example
FOR I = 0 TO 100 STEP 10
  Process(I)
NEXT I
@end example

@strong{Example 3: Backward FOR Loop**:
@example
FOR I = 10 TO 1 STEP -1
  Print I
NEXT I
@end example

@strong{Example 4: Nested FOR Loops**:
@example
FOR X = 0 TO 9
  FOR Y = 0 TO 9
    Grid(X, Y) = 0
  NEXT Y
NEXT X
@end example

@strong{Example 5: FOR with Different Types**:
@example
FOR I = 0 TO 255
  Flags = 0B1010
  Process(I)
NEXT I
@end example

@strong{Domain-Specific Features}:
FOR loops in Burgermistress support arbitrary step values. The compiler optimizes FOR to
efficient countdown loops when STEP is positive and EndValue is constant. Loop variables
are automatically scoped to the loop. FOR loops are ideal for array processing and game
entity iteration.

