@subsection Burgermistress Statement: SELECT-CASE

@cindex Burgermistress SELECT-CASE

SELECT-CASE provides multi-branch conditional logic based on a single expression value.

@strong{Syntax}:
@example
SELECT Expression
CASE Value1
  statements
CASE Value2, Value3
  statements
CASE ELSE
  statements
END SELECT
@end example

@strong{Example 1: Simple SELECT**:
@example
SELECT GameState
CASE PLAYING
  UpdateGame()
CASE PAUSED
  ShowPauseMenu()
CASE QUIT
  ExitGame()
END SELECT
@end example

@strong{Example 2: SELECT with Multiple Values**:
@example
SELECT ItemType
CASE SWORD, AXE, MACE
  EquipWeapon(Item)
CASE POTION, ELIXIR
  DrinkPotion(Item)
CASE KEY, CHEST
  LockItem(Item)
CASE ELSE
  DropItem(Item)
END SELECT
@end example

@strong{Example 3: SELECT with Numeric Values**:
@example
SELECT Difficulty
CASE 1
  EnemyHealth = 50
  EnemyDamage = 10
CASE 2
  EnemyHealth = 100
  EnemyDamage = 20
CASE 3
  EnemyHealth = 150
  EnemyDamage = 30
CASE ELSE
  EnemyHealth = 50
END SELECT
@end example

@strong{Example 4: SELECT with Different Types**:
@example
SELECT Flags
CASE 0B1010
  Action1()
CASE 0B1111
  Action2()
CASE 255
  Action3()
CASE ELSE
  DefaultAction()
END SELECT
@end example

@strong{Example 5: Complex SELECT**:
@example
SELECT EventType
CASE PLAYER_DAMAGE
  ProcessPlayerDamage()
CASE ENEMY_SPAWN
  ProcessEnemySpawn()
CASE DIALOGUE_START
  ProcessDialogue()
CASE LEVEL_COMPLETE
  CompleteLevelSequence()
CASE GAME_OVER
  ShowGameOverScreen()
CASE ELSE
  LogUnknownEvent(EventType)
END SELECT
@end example

@strong{Domain-Specific Features}:
SELECT-CASE is optimized to jump tables when test values are constants. Multiple values
per case enable grouping of related branches. Numeric types support efficient comparisons.
SELECT is cleaner than nested IF for multi-branch logic.

