@subsection Burgermistress Statement: EXIT

@cindex Burgermistress EXIT

The EXIT statement terminates loops prematurely.

@strong{Syntax}:
@example
EXIT DO
EXIT FOR
@end example

@strong{Example 1: Exit DO Loop**:
@example
DO
  Input(Command)
  IF Command = "QUIT" THEN
    EXIT DO
  END IF
LOOP
@end example

@strong{Example 2: Exit FOR Loop**:
@example
FOR I = 0 TO 1000
  IF Found(I) THEN
    EXIT FOR
  END IF
NEXT
@end example

@strong{Example 3: Exit in Nested Loops**:
@example
FOR X = 0 TO 9
  FOR Y = 0 TO 9
    IF Grid(X, Y) = TARGET THEN
      EXIT FOR
    END IF
  NEXT Y
  IF Found THEN
    EXIT FOR
  END IF
NEXT X
@end example

@strong{Example 4: Exit with Condition**:
@example
DO
  FrameCount = FrameCount + 1
  IF FrameCount > 6000 THEN  ' 100 seconds at 60 FPS
    EXIT DO
  END IF
LOOP
@end example

@strong{Example 5: Search Loop with Exit**:
@example
FOR I = 0 TO MAX-ENTITIES
  IF Entity(I).Type = PLAYER THEN
    PlayerIndex = I
    EXIT FOR
  END IF
NEXT
@end example

@strong{Domain-Specific Features}:
EXIT provides clean loop termination for search and processing loops. EXIT DO and EXIT FOR
specify which loop level to exit, supporting nested loop control. The compiler optimizes
EXIT to direct jump instructions.

